    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1923, Cromwell was named for Muscogee oilman Joe I. Cromwell, who platted the original town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cromwell%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cromwell was known as a wild and wooly town in the early 1920s, filled with saloons and outlaws.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cromwell%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "About 150 businesses operated in Cromwell during the 1920s, with many selling moonshine and narcotics to the surrounding area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cromwell%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
